            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0472" n="374" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg374"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/572: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva (Gilbert) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-11-29T14:00:00+01:00">November 29, 1932—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 29—9:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>344. General McCoy informs me
                    that Lytton has asked him to
                    remain in Geneva, subject to call, in connection with the forthcoming <pb
                        facs="0473" n="375" xml:id="pg375"/> meetings of the Assembly, and that he
                    is complying with this request of the Chairman of the Commission of Inquiry.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
